# minarch-gl core list (h700)
#
# One line per core pak: <tag>  <core name>  <default ROM folders, ";" separated>
#
# The tag is the pak directory name (Emus/<plat>/<TAG>.pak) and the namespace the
# installer owns; the core name is the <name>_libretro.so inside it and the first
# field of the pak's `version` file.
#
# tools/release.sh turns this table plus the pins in gles-cores/<plat>/makefile
# into core-list.json, the manifest the installer reads.  Cores are only ever
# added here: a core that stops being maintained keeps its line and its pin, so
# an installed copy stays recognisable and uninstallable.
#
# BIOS is not listed here: every core gets Bios/<TAG>/ (NextUI's convention, and
# what minarch hands to the core as its system directory), and how a core lays
# out the files inside it is the core's own business -- see the core's libretro
# documentation.  The installer only creates the empty tag directory.
#
# tag                      core                default ROM folders
LIBRETRO_FLYCAST           flycast             Sega Dreamcast;Sega Naomi
LIBRETRO_MUPEN64PLUS       mupen64plus_next    Nintendo 64
LIBRETRO_YABASANSHIRO      yabasanshiro        Sega Saturn;Sega Titan Video
LIBRETRO_SWANSTATION       swanstation         Sony PlayStation
LIBRETRO_PPSSPP            ppsspp              PlayStation Portable
